We are all three very full now.
There is no more food left on the table.
"That was a fantastic dinner, Maya," Sara says happily.
"How exactly do you make these meatballs?" she then asks.
"Is it very difficult?"
"No, it is actually quite easy," I answer.
"First you chop onions, and afterwards you mix the meat," I explain.
"I have a really good recipe on my phone."
"I will send a link to you tonight."
"Thank you very much, I would like to try that," Sara says.
We stand up from the small chairs.
Kasper begins to gather the empty plates.
"Should we take the plates out into the kitchen now?" he asks.
"Yes please."
"Just put them on the kitchen counter," I say.
We quickly clear the table together.
"But hey, next time it is my turn," Kasper says suddenly.
"Yes."
"Next time you must cook for us!"
Sara laughs.
"Exactly."
"And I promise that it will be good," he says.
We laugh and carry the rest of the things out into the kitchen.
